<title>AUSTRIA: TENNIS-GENERALI OPEN MEN'S RESULTS.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-GENERALI OPEN MEN'S RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>KITZBUEHEL, Austria 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of second</p>
<p>round matches at the $535,000 Generali Open men's tennis</p>
<p>tournament on Wednesday (prefix number denotes seeding):</p>
<p>Hernan Gumy (Argentina) beat 4-Gustavo Kuerten (Brazil) 6-1 6-3</p>
<p>13-Hendrik Dreekmann (Germany) beat Quino Munoz (Spain 6-0 6-1</p>
<p>14-Galo Blanco (Spain) beat Franco Squillari (Argentina) 6-3</p>
<p>6-2</p>
<p>10-Filip Dewulf (Belgium) beat Martin Sinner (Germany) 6-1 6-0</p>
<p>2-Yevgeny Kafelnikov (Russia) beat Fernando Meligeni (Brazil)</p>
<p>6-1 6-3</p>
<p>Bernd Karbacher (Germany) beat Jiri Novak (Czech Republic) 6-3</p>
<p>6-4</p>
<p>3-Alex Corretja (Spain) beat Lucas Arnold (Argentina) 6-2 6-7</p>
<p>(8-10) 6-4</p>
<p>Stefan Koubek (Austria) beat 5-Alberto Berasategui (Spain) 6-2</p>
<p>6-3</p>
<p>7-Hicham Arazi (Marocco) beat Gerald Mandl (Austria) 6-4 7-6</p>
<p>(7-4)</p>
<p>16-Renzo Furlan (Italy) beat Marcos Aurelio Gorriz (Spain) 6-2</p>
<p>6-4</p>
<p>Julian Alonso (Spain) beat 6-Bohdan Ulirach (Czech Republic)</p>
<p>6-2 6-3</p>
<p>Nicolas Lapentti (Ecuador) beat 12-Jeff Tarango (U.S.) 6-3 3-6</p>
<p>6-1</p>
<p>1-Thomas Muster (Austria) beat Carlos Costa (Spain) 6-3 6-1</p>
</text>
